# Private terms for the local privacy gate.
#
# This file is git-ignored and stays on this machine. The gate reads it on
# every run and blocks any line that contains one of the terms. The terms are
# also applied to commit messages, to annotated tag messages and to the path
# of every changed file.
#
# Add one term per line, for example:
#   client and supplier names
#   your IBANs, written with or without spaces
#   your KvK number, VAT number and BSN
#   your home address and private email addresses
#
# Your own name needs no entry. It is already public as the author of your
# commits and in LICENSE, and the gate never applies the denylist to LICENSE
# or to author and committer names. An entry for your own name would only
# block commit messages that mention it.
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and also ignores whitespace, so an IBAN can be
# written with or without spaces. Lines starting with # are comments. Terms
# shorter than 4 characters are ignored.
#
# Run scripts/install-hooks.sh to copy this file to .privacy-denylist and to
# put your own terms in the copy. The copy is never committed, so keep real
# terms out of this example file.
